# Root vs app/

Astra uses a **single main package**: **`app/`**. There is no dual root-vs-src structure to keep in sync.

- **`app/`**: Core application (main, interfaces, core systems, events, Discord, etc.). Put new features and application logic here.
- **Root**: Entry point (`run_astra.py`), `config/`, `scripts/`, `utils/`, `maintenance/`, and top-level packages like `astra_growth/`.

Run from project root with `PYTHONPATH=.` so that `app` and root modules resolve correctly (e.g. `run_astra.py` or `python -m app.main`).
